WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:02.152
Okay, I found the tasks in the queue.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.686
Yeah, the first attempt didn't finish.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.095
The page was the one that
stopped responding.

00:00:08.786 --> 00:00:11.789
The server kept generating the
report normally.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.825
Then another attempt came in and started
everything all over again.

00:00:15.194 --> 00:00:18.696
It's not a queue of different things,
it's the same thing multiple times.

00:00:19.065 --> 00:00:22.149
Including the same chart, which still
doesn't explain anything.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.354
And there's more.

00:00:23.804 --> 00:00:26.090
The service receiving the
calls already makes

00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:28.173
three attempts before returning an error.

00:00:28.623 --> 00:00:32.035
So, the new change is repeating an
operation that already repeats itself.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.641
Wait, does the background
process do that too?

00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:37.588
I'll send the logs.

00:00:38.184 --> 00:00:41.773
For now, nobody should press the
button—not even to check whether it improved.

